From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:50:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: fw_cache_maint switch for firmware data-cache
 maintenance

The M4 path inherited per-write dc ivac/cvac from the m1n1 Python shim,
which reached target memory through the proxy. Upstream G13/G14 shares
firmware objects coherently and orders them with barriers only, and G16
already relies on coherency for writeback user BOs. fw_cache_maint=0
skips data-line maintenance on firmware live writes and reads, write_low
and page initialization, keeping every barrier; page-table, TTB and
handoff cleans are unchanged. Default 1 keeps the current behaviour.

Folded in:
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 fw_cache_maint switch for firmware data cache maintenance
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 runtime fw_cache_maint toggle in debugfs

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 runtime fw_cache_maint toggle in debugfs]
asahi_m4/fw_cache_maint (0/1) overrides the boot parameter for
same-boot A/B; the write paths read it each time. Maintenance now
invalidates with dc civac, identical for clean lines and safe for lines
left dirty while maintenance was off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
